<http://data.silknow.org/object/fa2788ab-1c41-369c-a3a1-505fc00bea01>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Woven silk, Persia, 1736-1749."@en , "Woven silk with gold ground, small-scale repeated design of a man, in blue tunic and red hat, perched in a tree, shooting arrows at a pair of lions who are attacking his horse.\nCompound tabby weave, brocaded. Warp proportion: 4 main ends of Z-twisted pink silk, 1 binding end of Z-twisted apricot silk. Wefts: gold and silver thread (lamé twisted S on Z-twisted silk, yellow and white respectively), silk in green, yellow, blue, red, pink, lilac, brown and white."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/739ddd87-a27d-3c95-a173-c55fc211c8e7> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Woven silk, Persia, 1736-1749."@en , "Woven silk with gold ground, small-scale repeated design of a man, in blue tunic and red hat, perched in a tree, shooting arrows at a pair of lions who are attacking his horse.\nCompound tabby weave, brocaded. Warp proportion: 4 main ends of Z-twisted pink silk, 1 binding end of Z-twisted apricot silk. Wefts: gold and silver thread (lamé twisted S on Z-twisted silk, yellow and white respectively), silk in green, yellow, blue, red, pink, lilac, brown and white."@en ;
